        "# Runtime Feedback Loops Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `run_with_feedback(command, agent_note)` that wraps `subprocess.run`, captures stdout/stderr/exit/duration, truncates deterministically, appends to `feedback_record.jsonl`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A small loader that streams the JSONL into a Python list."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that runs three commands (success, failure, slow) and prints the last record per command."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: three feedback records appended to `feedback_record.jsonl`, the last one of each printed inline. Tail the file across re-runs to see the loop accumulate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a `cwd` field per record so the same command run from different directories is distinguishable.\n2. Add a `redaction` step that strips lines matching `^Bearer ` or `password=`. Test on a fixture record.\n3. Cap total `feedback_record.jsonl` size at 1 MB by rotating to `.1`, `.2` files. Defend the rotation policy.\n4. Add a `parent_command_id` so retry chains are visible: which command produced the input that the next command consumed.\n5. Pipe the JSONL into a tiny TUI that highlights the latest non-zero exit. Eight key features the TUI must show to be useful in a review."
      ]
    }
